<% content_for :title, "BMI Calculator — whizwheel" %>

<%#
  BMI calculator page — regenerated from spec issue #53 against DESIGN.md (BLEND).

  Two unit systems (US / Metric) select the server-side formula and which height
  affordance the page collects. The page is server-rendered and progressively enhanced
  (DESIGN.md §0): it works WITHOUT JS, posting over Turbo and re-rendering the #result
  region in place. The canonical posted fields are always inputs[weight], inputs[height]
  (total inches for US, centimetres for metric) and the checked inputs[unit_system].

  Picker choice (the picker rule, DESIGN.md §4 "Mode picker"): the unit system is a
  variant selector with N=2 short labels (US / Metric, ≤12 chars) — and DESIGN.md names
  "BMI's US|Metric" as a canonical SEGMENTED CONTROL. So it is the connected horizontal
  track (the same vocabulary as the Percentage page's increase/decrease toggle), NOT a
  wrapping pill row and NOT the .mode-option list (which is reserved for N ≥ 4 or
  multi-word labels). It stays a native radio <fieldset>/<legend> posting
  inputs[unit_system]; the .peer:checked baseline paints the active half with no JS.

  Progressive enhancement of height (DESIGN.md §0): without JS the user types a single
  height value into the canonical field (total inches for US, cm for metric). With JS the
  bmi_controller offers US users friendlier feet + inches helper fields (no name → never
  posted), summing them into the canonical inputs[height], and swaps the weight unit affix.

  Layout (DESIGN.md §3): an input column + a results panel (≈380px 1fr), one column on
  mobile. Spacing — segmented halves tight (gap-1, Affix tier), stacked fields space-y-5,
  major blocks mt-8 (Section tier), column gutter/card padding gap-8 / p-7–p-8 (Layout).
%>

<header class="max-w-2xl">
  <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent">Fitness &amp; Health</p>
  <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.035em] text-ink">BMI Calculator</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
    Your Body Mass Index from weight and height, in US or metric units, with the World
    Health Organization adult classification band. Every answer is computed server-side.
  </p>
</header>

<div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[380px_1fr]">
  <%# ── Input column ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── %>
  <section class="rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface p-7 shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)] sm:p-8">
    <%= form_with url: "/calculators/bmi", scope: :inputs, method: :post,
          data: { controller: "bmi", bmi_weight_units_value: { us: "lb", metric: "kg" }.to_json } do |f| %>

      <%# Unit-system picker — SEGMENTED CONTROL (DESIGN.md §4 picker rule: N=2, short
          labels; DESIGN.md names BMI's US|Metric as the canonical example). One connected,
          bg-tinted, bordered track; the two systems are halves (.direction-pill) tight on
          the Affix tier (gap-1 — parts of one control). The active half lifts to surface
          white via .peer:checked (no-JS baseline) and .is-active (the controller's
          paintPills hook). Native radio <fieldset>/<legend> posting inputs[unit_system]. %>
      <fieldset>
        <legend class="text-xs font-bold text-label">Unit system</legend>
        <div class="mt-1.5 flex gap-1 rounded-[11px] border border-border-input bg-bg p-1">
          <% [["us", "US units"], ["metric", "Metric units"]].each_with_index do |(value, text), i| %>
            <%= f.radio_button :unit_system, value,
                  checked: i.zero?,
                  class: "peer sr-only",
                  data: { bmi_target: "systemInput", action: "bmi#select" } %>
            <%= f.label :unit_system, text, value: value,
                  class: "direction-pill",
                  data: { bmi_target: "pill", system: value } %>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <%# Fields — weight is shared (its unit affix swaps lb↔kg); height is per-system.
          Stacked tier: space-y-5 down the column (DESIGN.md §3). %>
      <div class="mt-8 space-y-5">
        <%# Weight — shared across both systems; the affix swaps with the mode. Affix tier
            (gap-2) sits the unit beside its field. shrink-0 keeps the affix from
            compressing when the field is wide. %>
        <div>
          <%= f.label :weight, "Weight", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_weight" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <%= f.number_field :weight, id: "inputs_weight", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                  min: "0", placeholder: "0", class: "field-input" %>
            <span class="w-7 shrink-0 text-sm font-bold text-label" data-bmi-target="weightUnit" aria-hidden="true">lb</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# Height (metric) — a single centimetres field carrying the canonical
            inputs[height] name. Hidden by default in the markup so the no-JS baseline
            shows exactly ONE height affordance (US, the default system) and the two
            inputs[height] fields never both post and clobber each other; the controller
            toggles which system's block shows. (No-JS users compute in the default US
            units; switching systems is the JS enhancement — DESIGN.md §0.) %>
        <div data-bmi-target="field" data-bmi-systems="metric" hidden>
          <%= f.label :height, "Height", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_height_cm" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <%= f.number_field :height, id: "inputs_height_cm", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                  min: "0", placeholder: "0", class: "field-input" %>
            <span class="w-7 shrink-0 text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">cm</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# Height (US) — exactly ONE affordance per path (DESIGN.md §0 progressive
            enhancement):
              • No JS  → the canonical "Total height in inches" field (visible by default);
                         the ft+in helpers stay hidden (inert without the controller).
              • With JS → bmi_controller reveals the ft+in helpers and hides the raw
                         total-inches field, summing ft×12 + in into the canonical field. %>
        <div data-bmi-target="field" data-bmi-systems="us">
          <%# Feet + inches helpers — hidden until JS reveals them. NO name → never posted;
              the controller writes their sum into the canonical height field below. Each
              has its own <label> (DESIGN.md §6 — a label for every input). Wrapping pair
              on the Grouped-wrapping tier (gap-x-3 gap-y-4). %>
          <div data-bmi-target="feetInches" hidden>
            <span class="field-label">Height</span>
            <div class="mt-1.5 grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-3 gap-y-4">
              <div>
                <%= f.label :feet, "Feet", class: "sr-only", for: "inputs_height_feet" %>
                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                  <%= f.number_field :feet, name: nil, id: "inputs_height_feet", step: "any",
                        inputmode: "decimal", min: "0", placeholder: "0", class: "field-input",
                        data: { bmi_target: "feet", action: "bmi#syncHeight" } %>
                  <span class="w-7 shrink-0 text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">ft</span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div>
                <%= f.label :inches, "Inches", class: "sr-only", for: "inputs_height_inches" %>
                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                  <%= f.number_field :inches, name: nil, id: "inputs_height_inches", step: "any",
                        inputmode: "decimal", min: "0", placeholder: "0", class: "field-input",
                        data: { bmi_target: "inches", action: "bmi#syncHeight" } %>
                  <span class="w-7 shrink-0 text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">in</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <%# Canonical total-inches field — the no-JS affordance (visible by default), the
              JS write-target (the controller hides it and writes the summed total here). %>
          <div data-bmi-target="totalInches">
            <%= f.label :height, "Total height in inches", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_height_in" %>
            <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
              <%= f.number_field :height, id: "inputs_height_in", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                    min: "0", placeholder: "0", class: "field-input",
                    data: { bmi_target: "usHeight" } %>
              <span class="w-7 shrink-0 text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">in</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <%# Submit — Section tier above; primary coral button (DESIGN.md §4). %>
      <%= f.submit "Calculate",
            class: "mt-8 w-full cursor-pointer rounded-[13px] bg-primary px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-surface shadow-sm transition-opacity hover:opacity-90 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent" %>
    <% end %>
  </section>

  <%# ── Results panel (the Turbo target) ─────────────────────────────────── %>
  <section id="result" aria-live="polite">
    <%= render "calculators/result", calc: nil %>
  </section>
</div>
